Cinematographers Barry Ackroyd and Christopher Ross are set to be honored by the British Society of Cinematographers . The Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences will receive the BSC Bert Easey Technical Achievement Award.

Ackroyd, whose credits include &#x201C;The Hurt Locker&#x201D; and &#x201C;United 93,&#x201D; as well as collaborations with director Ken Loach, including &#x201C;Sweet Sixteen&#x201D; and &#x201C;The Wind That Shakes the Barley will receive the BSC's highest honor, the Lifetime Achievement Award, in recognition of a career spanning more than 40 years across film and television. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Ross will receive the Society's BSC John Alcott Award, sponsored by ARRI. This award recognizes an individual for their services to the Society.

Ross, who served as President of the British Society of Cinematographers between 2022 and 2026, helped revamp the BSC Education Series, the rejuvenation of the Q&A series, the restructuring of the Society's committees and overseeing growth in both membership and diversity.

The Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences will receive the BSC Bert Easey Technical Achievement Award. Celebrating its 100th anniversary as an organization in 2027, the Academy has been a leading force in recognizing technical achievement and innovation, enabling and supporting filmmakers and contributing to the development of technical standards across our industry.

Among the Academy's many achievements are its contribution to the standardization of the 4:3 aspect ratio in the 1920s and 1930s, now commonly known as the &#x201C;Academy Ratio&#x201D;; the introduction of the Scientific and Technical Awards, which recognize the technicians and companies whose innovations make the films we see today possible; and the development of the Academy Color Encoding System (ACES), which provides a global, open-source standard for color management. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The Academy has also featured many technology-related exhibitions and programs at the Academy Museum of Motion Pictures and launched the Academy Marquee Theater List, which aims to celebrate cinemas that exemplify the moviegoing experience around the world, through audio-visual fidelity, diverse programming, community engagement and more.

In a statement, Oliver Stapleton BSC, President of the British Society of Cinematographers, commented: &#x201C;It is a great pleasure for us to recognize four very deserving recipients at this year's BSC Awards. Each, in their own way, has made an outstanding contribution to our industry and to the wider world of cinematography.&#x201D; He continued, &#x201C;Barry Ackroyd's extraordinary body of work has helped shape modern filmmaking and his contribution to cinematography over many decades is truly remarkable. Christopher Ross has given so much to the BSC, not only through his outstanding work as a cinematographer but also through his commitment, leadership and dedication during his time as President.&#x201D;

Stapleton said, &#x201C;The Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences has played an invaluable role in championing the art and science of filmmaking, celebrating technical innovation and supporting the creative community.&#x201D;

Pat McEnallay is set to receive the BSC Special Achievement Award. McEnallay has been a champion of young filmmakers and a trailblazer in the development of sustainable solutions for filmmaking.

McEnallay began his career working with companies such as Lee Lighting, Agfa and Panalux, supporting the development of new technologies and helping young cinematographers access the equipment they needed to make short films. Among those he supported were Lol Crawley, Ross and Ed Wild. He also serves as Co-Chair of the BSC Sustainability Committee and continues to support and enable the next generation of filmmakers.

Stapleton said, &#x201C;Pat McEnallay's generosity, enthusiasm and determination to support the next generation of filmmakers, alongside his pioneering work in sustainability, make him a hugely deserving recipient. What unites all four is their generosity of spirit and their commitment to making our industry better. On behalf of the BSC, I would like to congratulate them all and thank them for everything they have contributed to our craft and our community.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The awards will be presented alongside the competitive awards at the 71st British Society of Cinematographers Awards on Feb. 6, 2027. The ceremony will be hosted by Edith Bowman and will take place in the Great Room at the Grosvenor House Hotel.

Jennifer Lopez has entered her &#x201C;happy era.&#x201D;

The singer-dancer-actress makes that perfectly clear in her new concert film, &#x201C;The JLo Show: Live in Las Vegas,&#x201D; with self-deprecating jokes about her much tabloidized love life.

&#x201C;If you take life too seriously, you'll be a miserable person,&#x201D; Lopez tells me during a recent conversation over Zoom. &#x201C;You have to find the humor in things, and you have to be honest with who you are &#x2014; not just all the great things about who you are, but all of the things that you you've done and the choices you've made that were questionable. We&#x2019;ve all made those.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories 'The Comeback King' Trailer: Glen Powell Is a Washed-Up Country Star in Judd Apatow's New Comedy Jessica Chastain Returning to Broadway in New Play 'Lost Lear'

Today, Lopez says, her life at 57 is &#x201C;unencumbered with any toxicity, it&#x2019;s unencumbered with any other kind of relationship in my life that is not healthy for me and so it&#x2019;s only the relationship with myself that I&#x2019;m dealing with right now.&#x201D;

&#x201C;I have gotten closer to God spiritually,&#x201D; she continues. &#x201C;I have gotten more self-aware, more appreciative of the little girl who grew up in the Bronx in front of that television &#x2026; It&#x2019;s been a very happy time and I think it may surprise people because they think, oh God, all this stuff happened again and it&#x2019;s like, no, no. It was the best thing that ever happened to me, and I&#x2019;m really grateful for where I am right now.&#x201D;

